hundreds of miles across the empire and force you to speak Quechua, their language, you know, if they want to. So local kind of warlords have taken control in some areas. People have thrown off the Inca sun cult and gone back to their old gods and things. And as John Heming, in his brilliant book about the conquest of Peru, says, Manco had to try to restore the sort of cult of the Inca, to take over control of the administration, to assert his primacy as supreme ruler. He had to revive the prestige of Kusko. He had to revive the prestige of the official religion, all of this kind of thing.
帝国各地数百英里之外，并强迫你说克丘亚语，也就是他们的语言。所以当地的一些军阀在某些地区夺取了控制权。人们抛弃了印加太阳崇拜，回到了他们古老的神灵等等。正如约翰·海明在他关于征服秘鲁的精彩著作中所说，曼科必须努力恢复印加的某种崇拜，接管行政管理权，确立他作为最高统治者的首要地位。他必须重振库斯科的威望。他必须重振官方宗教的威望，所有这些事情。

11
00:05:53.000 --> 00:06:42.000
Now, the Spanish, up to a point, are useful allies in this. He presumably sees them as so many people do in these sort of stories as merely a new factor in the existing kind of political landscape of Peru and one that he can harness and use. So Dominic, at this point, Manco assumes that everything can carry on pretty much as it always has done. He doesn't think that the Spanish essentially have changed everything. No, because we're talking about very small numbers of people. I mean, at the end of this decade, the Spanish did a census of their own population in New Castile, as they called it, and we were talking about 4,000 people. So at this stage, we're probably talking about half that, something like that. I mean, a tiny number, right?
现在，西班牙人在某种程度上是这方面的有用盟友。他大概像许多人在这类故事中所做的那样，仅仅把他们看作秘鲁现有政治格局中的一个新因素，一个他可以利用和驾驭的因素。所以多米尼克，在这一点上，曼科认为一切都可以像往常一样继续下去。他不认为西班牙人基本上改变了一切。不，因为我们谈论的是非常少的人。我的意思是，在这个十年结束时，西班牙人对他们在新卡斯蒂利亚（他们这样称呼它）的人口进行了普查，我们谈论的是4000人。所以在这个阶段，我们可能谈论的是这个数字的一半，诸如此类。我的意思是，一个极小的数字，对吧？

12
00:06:42.000 --> 00:07:30.000
In an empire of 12 million people, 2,000 maximum, probably hundreds at this stage. So why would he think differently? These are elite mercenaries to whom he owes his throne, but they're not going to be a factor forever, and there's probably not that many more of them. And of course, in this, he is completely nuttly wrong. Anyway, at first the signs are all good. He builds himself a new palace in Kusco. And interestingly, quite a difference, I think, with Mexico. The Spanish don't seem terribly keen on pushing the program of Christianisation. So, you know, Manco is completely free to continue with the religious rituals that enshrine his primacy as the Sapa Inca. There's a lovely description by a young priest called Christobald de Molina of a ploughing festival in April 1535. It's one of the
在一个拥有1200万人口的帝国里，最多2000人，在这个阶段可能只有几百人。所以他为什么要另想呢？这些是他欠下王位的精英雇佣兵，但他们不会永远是一个因素，而且可能没有那么多。当然，在这点上，他完全大错特错了。无论如何，起初迹象都很好。他在库斯科为自己建造了一座新宫殿。有趣的是，我认为与墨西哥有很大的不同。西班牙人似乎对推行基督教化计划并不太热衷。所以，你知道，曼科完全可以自由地继续进行那些确立他作为萨帕·印加首要地位的宗教仪式。一位名叫克里斯托瓦尔·德·莫利纳的年轻牧师对1535年4月的犁地节有一个可爱的描述。这是我们拥有的

13
